      "post_id": "63509",
      "author_handle": "kristag",
      "date_as_displayed": "Posted 18 years 1 month ago",
      "body": "I'm planning to breastfeed this time (all being well) but also would like to express too so Mike can join in and do feeds.\nMy question is really daft so forgive me!\nIf I feed from one side at a time, would I express from the other side?  Then what happens at next feed, with the expressed breast have enough milk for baby?\nLast time I just expressed full time as Jas wouldn't breastfeed due to being premature so I used to do both sides each time.  With wanting to breastfeed this time and express too, I'm confused... 🤔",
      "permalink": "https://www.justparents.co.uk/forums/topic-6465/#63509",
      "raw_file": "_raw/forums-deep/justparents/responses/8e554907fef65cef29f2.html",
      "page_url": "https://www.justparents.co.uk/forums/topic-6465/",
      "role": "original_post",
      "original_post_id": "63509"
    },
    {
      "post_id": "63513",
      "author_handle": "angelsmom",
      "date_as_displayed": "Posted 18 years 1 month ago",
      "body": "express from the opposite side to last feed then baby will feed again on the same as before. (ie feed right, express left, feed right.) its all just about releiving the pressure really.",
      "permalink": "https://www.justparents.co.uk/forums/topic-6465/#63513",
      "raw_file": "_raw/forums-deep/justparents/responses/8e554907fef65cef29f2.html",
